# What a store actually installs. `export-ignore` applies to `git archive`,
# which is what GitHub builds the zipball from, so this is the dist package —
# roughly half the repository is development scaffolding with no business on a
# production server.
#
# `--prefer-source` clones the repository and ignores all of this, so the test
# and demo suites stay available to anyone who wants to run them.
#
# resources/ must never be listed here: the EOL manifest is runtime data, and
# the lifecycle advisories read it from the installed package.
/.github/           export-ignore
/bin/               export-ignore
/demo/              export-ignore
/docs/              export-ignore
/tests/             export-ignore
/.gitattributes     export-ignore
/.gitignore         export-ignore
/phpstan.neon       export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md          export-ignore
